          "text": "In the general discussion channel, several topics came up throughout the day. Sam announced that a Zeroclaw community call was live, inviting members interested in how the project supports the broader crypto ecosystem. A user named Faouzi122 raised a technical question directed at developers building AI agents that allocate capital into liquidity pool positions, asking how they handle impermanent loss calculations and breakeven points before committing funds to a pool, specifically whether they hardcode formulas, use an SDK, or skip the check entirely. The question was framed as an attempt to determine if this is a genuine ongoing pain point in the space. A user named Angelina directed criticism at project leadership, tagging moderators Shaw and Kenk, claiming the project's decline began before the bear market due to immature leadership. Shagun asked who to contact regarding listing proposals, receiving a dismissive reaction from other members. Troseddol and Mint from Action Model both reached out seeking partnership contacts, with Mint specifically identifying themselves as representing Action Model and asking how to pursue partnership discussions.",
